  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 builds `Lasso(alpha, max_iter=10000, tol=1e-3, selection='random')` with `random_state` unset (global numpy stream). The v2 `lasso` predictor has the same solver settings (`non_tunable_hyperparameters`) and pins `random_state=0`, which makes a v2 fit reproducible where 1.6.1 draws a different coordinate order per process. With the global stream seeded with 0 on the 1.6.1 side the random coordinate order is identical and the fitted coefficients agree to float32 precision (class forward) with the unmodified preset.",
    "The 1.6.1 default (first grid point) and the v2 default are both alpha=1.0 (the 1.6.1 grid is 1, 0.8, 0.6, 0.4, 0.1, 0.01, 5); the v2 search space is log-uniform in [1e-4, 10].",
    "1.6.1 selects the `landmark_genes` list while loading; the v2 `Lasso` preset selects the same list with `scaledGeneExpression(gene_list=landmark_genes)`. The synthetic gene names are in no shipped list, so both sides get a pre-selected matrix and the selection itself is not compared here.",
    "Features agree to float32 precision (class forward): v2 holds them as float32, 1.6.1 as float64."
  ],
